  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved 0.591 acc / 0.573 F1, a substantial +10.6 pt gain over the singleprofile baseline (config_001, 0.485 acc). This strongly indicates that multiprofile aggregation is the key lever for RNA performance. Uncertainty: we do not yet know whether transformer aggregation outperforms simple avgpool for the same encoder and profile setting. Question tested: config_003 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding model_setting, profile_setting, and rna_encoder identical to config_002, cleanly isolating the aggregation effect. Why this is the best next experiment: (1) it is a single-variable comparison extending the strongest finding, (2) the answer directly determines which aggregation to carry into all subsequent multimodal experiments (configs 020/021, 026/027, etc.), (3) it is low-risk since RNA already performs well, and (4) under a limited budget, resolving the aggregation choice before adding modality complexity avoids confounding multiple design decisions simultaneously."
}

